.TH GIT-KITTEN 1 "2026-08-08" "git-kitten 0.1.0" "Git Kitten Manual"
.SH NAME
git-kitten \- opt-in kitten diff (kitty) as a git subcommand
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git kitten diff
[\fI<git diff args>\fR]
.br
.B git kitten diff
\fI<A>\fR \fI<B>\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Open your git diffs in kitty's side-by-side viewer
.RB ( "kitten diff" ).
It is opt-in: a
.B git kitten
subcommand you run when you want it, with no changes to your git config.
.PP
.I <A>
and
.I <B>
are anything you would give
.BR "git diff" :
commits, branches, ranges, or paths. Inside a repository all
.B git diff
argument forms are supported; they are handed to
.B git difftool --dir-diff
so the two sides are materialized into temporary directories and opened once.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B git kitten diff
Unstaged changes.
.TP
.B git kitten diff --staged
Staged changes.
.TP
.B git kitten diff HEAD
All uncommitted changes.
.TP
.B git kitten diff HEAD~1 HEAD
Between two commits.
.TP
.B git kitten diff main feature
Between two branches.
.TP
.B git kitten diff HEAD~1 HEAD -- path
Scoped to a path.
.SH NOTES
Passing two revisions compares two commits and ignores the working tree; pass a
single revision (for example
.BR "git kitten diff origin/master" )
to compare a commit against your working tree.
.PP
To compare two arbitrary files or directories you do not need git or this
wrapper; use
.B kitten diff a.txt b.txt
directly.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-diff (1),
.BR git-difftool (1),
.BR kitty (1)
